{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1099429-how-to-make-focused-mage-sight-scenes-more-engaging","id":1099429,"title":"How to make Focused Mage Sight scenes more engaging.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-02T03:16:40-07:00","id":1099429,"title":"How to make Focused Mage Sight scenes more engaging.","content":"Hi all<br /> <br /> So I have a broad plan for my first session of 2nd edition Mage, and was sitting down to set the Opacity of my first few Mysteries and I got to thinking about what happens when my 5 players come into contact with them. <br /> <br /> The system doesn't seem overly engaging at first glance, lots and lots of dice rolls in exchange for occasional clues. <br /> <br /> Was hoping for some advice from people who have used the system. How do I make this interesting enough to keep my players engaged?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T03:26:39-07:00","id":1099430,"title":"","content":"There's a reason the book suggests not jacking the Opacity up too high.<br /> <br /> Other than that, Mage Sight is a brute force approach to sussing out answers, think about how to narrate that when cracking a level of Opacity. Narrative is -the- tool for making any level of dice rolling interesting whether it's one roll or one thousand.<br /> <br /> You can also break up MS rolls by applying pressure from other sources to hurry it along or interrupt it and force them to come back to it later.<br /> <br /> You should probably never find yourself in a situation where your player just rolls and you don't have anything happen or lack an interesting description for what happens as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T05:14:52-07:00","id":1099455,"title":"","content":"Good points, I will keep this first mystery fairly low, to see how the players get on with the idea.<br /> <br /> My main concern is having a number of players sat around while those who have the relevant Arcana go to town. Hopefully between a fairly low Opacity, some good descriptions, and reminding the other players that they could be using other forms of investigation, I can keep the pace going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T05:29:58-07:00","id":1099462,"title":"","content":"It's possible for a Mage to get deep info without MS you know, that's what spells are for. If your other players have an idea for a different angle of investigation then see if you can make it work. If it can, and they succeed you can let them provide that information to the guys using MS and grant an equipment bonus or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T16:59:40-07:00","id":1102652,"title":"","content":"As a storyteller, I enjoy Mysteries that reveal things at different levels. It feels fun to have tid-not to share along the way, occasionally having a Mystery misleading hints and clues at higher levels, which are contradicted as deliberate obfuscation (likely Prime veiling or abysmal shenanigans) or will clarify something vague in an unexpected way (because the journey to the Truth can be naturally misleading sometimes). The main thing is I enjoy the reveal, as a player and the storyteller, and that's why I like Mysteries but make sure I spread out the reveal for my own personal taste. Another thing I do is set prerequisites to proceed to the next level of Opacity, which is implied but not explicit in the rules. For example it is implied you have &quot;access&quot; to the Mystery to examine it but what does that mean for each Mystery, and how can apply to each level of Opacity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T17:34:12-07:00","id":1102660,"title":"","content":"I've actually personally just ditched the Opacity / Mage Sight rules in their entirty, and have been using a modified version of the Investigation rules in the CofD core book. Not only do I find those rules more engaging and quick, but also they encourage different players to come at the Mystery from different angles, whereas the current rules tend to support just one mage, in my experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T06:56:19-07:00","id":1102791,"title":"","content":"One thing I am looking at doing is letting my players work together to bring down the Opacity of certain mysteries. For example in the last session I had an Opacity 3 mystery that could be interacted with using both Life and Mind. I let both my Mastigos and Thrysus players work together, alternating rolls and reducing the mysteries Opacity together. The players all seemed to prefer this method, so I am gonna roll with it, I just need to come up with a sensible way of capping the number of rolls before the Mystery gets tainted with mages Nimbus's (Nimbi?).]<br /> <br /> Any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T18:06:00-07:00","id":1102967,"title":"","content":"In addition to its insight into how Mage Sight will operate once Signs of Sorcery is released, the development materials on Mage Sight provide advice on how to improve the system of Focused Mage Sight. It's actually pretty helpful, and suggests whether you should increase/decrease Potency in certain stituations, such as perhaps a -1 or -2 to Opacity if the Mystery is central to the plot and necessary for advancement, or a well-catelogued Phenomenon.<br /> <br /> It also suggests the possibility of incremental information, granting insight into the Mystery as Opacity is decreased.<br /> So even if you can't get it all the way down to 0, you still feel you've learned something as you progress, which can help you investigate further.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9ejlGcDYtN3hZTWs/view\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9ejlGcDYtN3hZTWs/view\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9ejlGcDYtN3hZTWs/view\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9ejlGcDYtN3hZTWs/view </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}